            %p
          where by suggestive slight abuse of notation,
          %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
            %semantics
              %mrow
                %msub
                  %mi f
                  %mi i
              %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_i
          denotes the evident (co-)
          %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extensions"}> extensions
          \.
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              The first line is immediate on (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+element"}> generalized
              )
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elements"} elements
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_{-1}
              becomes
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+function"} injective
              when
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/restriction"} restricted
              to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi coker
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≡
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi im
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} coker(f_{-2}) \equiv A_{-1}/im(f_{-2})
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_{1}
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surjective+map"} surjective
              onto its image. The second line is clearly equal to the first line by exactness.
          %p
            In the following, for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi f
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \overset{f}{\longrightarrow} A
            any morphism, we abbreviate its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cokernel"} cokernel
            by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi X
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi coker
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  A/X \;\coloneqq\; coker(f)
                  \\,.
          .num_lemma
            %h6#lemma Lemma
            %p For
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    A \to B \to C \to 0
            %p
              an exact sequence in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
              and for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to B
              any morphism in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒜
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    A \to B/X \to C/X \to 0
            %p is a short exact sequence.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p We have an exact sequence of complexes of length 2
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mn 0
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi id
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mn 0
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi C
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    0 &amp;\to&amp; X &amp;\stackrel{id}{\to}&amp; X &amp;\to&amp; 0
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp; &amp; \downarrow &amp; &amp; \downarrow &amp; &amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    A &amp;\to&amp; B &amp;\to&amp; C &amp;\to&amp; 0
                    }
            %p
              and the exact sequence to be demonstrated is degreewise the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cokernel"} cokernel
              of this sequence. So the statement reduces to the fact that forming cokernels is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+exact+functor"} right exact functor
          %p
            (cf.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Wise11"} Wise 2011
          .num_lemma
            %h6#lemma_2 Lemma
            %p For
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    0 \to A \to B \to C
            %p
              an exact sequence and
